From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theo Slater <theoslater1@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:53:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView: Report pages that stop answering input

Watch key presses, clicks and wheel events sent to the page. When one
has gone unanswered for 8 seconds, report the page as unresponsive
through on_page_unresponsive_changed, and report it again once the
page catches up or the view navigates away.

The wait only counts while the page could answer: not while it is
hidden, loading, showing a dialog, paused in the debugger, or crashed.
Showing a dialog or pausing in the debugger also stops watching the
input sent before, since the page is busy with the user. The embedder
can keep waiting, which starts the 8 seconds over, or terminate the
process holding the oldest unanswered input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
